WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.155 --> 00:00:00.988
(audience applauding)
- All right,

00:00:00.988 --> 00:00:02.086
welcome back everybody.

00:00:02.086 --> 00:00:04.320
After a heated game of A Quiet Case,

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.408
back with The Chicks,
everybody give it up for them.

00:00:06.408 --> 00:00:07.899
(Kelly and audience applauding)

00:00:07.899 --> 00:00:09.367
And we're also still hanging out with

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:10.328
(audience applauding)
Matt Iseman,

00:00:10.328 --> 00:00:12.790
host of "American Ninja Warriors",

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:15.520
which begins a new season
this evening on NBC.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.939
(audience applauding)
So, had y'all ever met before?

00:00:18.939 --> 00:00:21.180
- We hadn't and I'd been a fan,

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.760
but it was cool watching
them just destroy you

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:24.820
and be heartless about it.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.289
- You know what, sir?
- Because they seem so nice.

00:00:26.289 --> 00:00:27.150
(all laughing)
- I can't wait to

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.650
kick your behind after the show.

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.520
You are my friend, sir.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:32.620
So wait, so you're from Denver.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:33.453
- Yeah.
- I actually didn't remember

00:00:33.453 --> 00:00:34.306
that you were from Colorado.

00:00:34.306 --> 00:00:35.330
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- That's awesome.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.610
So, how often do you get back to Denver?

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:37.800
Do you ever get back?
- I get back

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.140
probably seven or eight times a year.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:40.973
- [Kelly] Oh, that's good.

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:44.120
- I've found this place,
five star service to stay at.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.148
It's my parents' house.

00:00:45.148 --> 00:00:47.480
(all laughing)
It is, it is incredible.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.690
I go back there and this,
so my childhood bedroom

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.800
is unchanged since June
of '89, when I graduated

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:54.633
from high school.
- What?

00:00:54.633 --> 00:00:56.070
- Oh my.
- It is a time capsule.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.600
- Wow.
- You open the door,

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.709
you can smell the Drakkar Noir, it is-

00:00:59.709 --> 00:01:01.359
(all laughing)

00:01:01.359 --> 00:01:04.010
And so, that's, this was across,

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:08.190
this has been across
from my bed since '86.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.558
Every night, it's Arnold,

00:01:09.558 --> 00:01:11.245
♪ Go to sleep ♪

00:01:11.245 --> 00:01:12.370
(audience laughing)
- Oh my God, wait,

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:13.930
and "Predator", that was that (growling),

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:15.083
that sound, yeah.
- Yeah, that was it,

00:01:15.083 --> 00:01:15.916
that was it.
- I love "Predator".

00:01:15.916 --> 00:01:18.357
- And now we're friends,
and every time I tell him,

00:01:18.357 --> 00:01:20.370
"I had your poster on my bedroom wall",

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:22.957
he's like, "That's not even
creepy a little bit, Iseman.

00:01:22.957 --> 00:01:24.101
(all laughing)

00:01:24.101 --> 00:01:26.708
I wish I would've had your
poster on my bedroom wall."

00:01:26.708 --> 00:01:28.700
- [Kelly] (laughing) That
is an amazing impression!

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.830
- Oh, it's something, my mom,

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:32.027
people will come to the house and they go,

00:01:32.027 --> 00:01:34.120
"Oh, it's like you have
a 13 year old son."

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.650
I'm like, I do stand up comedy

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.781
and talk about ninjas, you kinda do, Mom.

00:01:37.781 --> 00:01:39.080
(audience laughing)
- Oh my gosh,

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:40.530
that's amazing.
- Yeah.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.363
- People would love that.

00:01:41.363 --> 00:01:43.100
What kind of posters did y'all have?

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:47.383
- Hmm, my whole wall
above my bed was Bon Jovi-

00:01:47.383 --> 00:01:49.754
- Oh!
- Bon Jovi and Sebastian Bach.

00:01:49.754 --> 00:01:50.587
(Natalie and audience laughing)

00:01:50.587 --> 00:01:51.950
- Oh my God, I love that.
- The greatest front man

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:53.663
of a heavy metal band of all time.

00:01:53.663 --> 00:01:54.580
I remember the year that-
- And some Axl Rose.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.050
I had some Axl Rose.
- I love Axl,

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.400
Guns and Roses, well, what about y'all?

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:58.640
- Jim Morrison-
- Oh.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.358
was in silk, above my bed.

00:02:00.358 --> 00:02:01.910
(all laughing)
- Love it.

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:02.930
What about you?

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:06.519
- I had Adam Ant and some banjo
players, which is so lame.

00:02:06.519 --> 00:02:08.690
(all laughing)
- I love that,

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:09.523
I love that.

00:02:09.523 --> 00:02:11.559
- [Matt] Steve Martin is
nodding along right now.

00:02:11.559 --> 00:02:12.600
- Yeah.
- I don't believe

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.050
banjo players had posters.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:16.068
- Bon Jovi.
- They had posters.

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:17.668
- His hair was amazing in the '80s.

00:02:17.668 --> 00:02:18.876
- Oh yeah, very good.
- Still.

00:02:18.876 --> 00:02:20.480
- It is still amazing.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.730
- Okay, so what's going
on, it's season 14, right?

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:23.563
- [Matt] Yes.

00:02:23.563 --> 00:02:24.396
- So, what's happening that's different

00:02:24.396 --> 00:02:25.229
in "American Ninja Warrior"?

00:02:25.229 --> 00:02:27.010
- Well, it just keeps getting bigger.

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:29.480
It keeps getting harder,
and they keep figuring

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:30.520
out a way to get through it.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:33.880
We, last season, we lowered the age to 15

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.540
to get on the show.
- Oh, so you have kids like

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:36.414
kicking adults behinds?

00:02:36.414 --> 00:02:38.094
- They are, Kelly!
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:38.094 --> 00:02:38.927
It is, I mean-

00:02:38.927 --> 00:02:39.760
- That is so sad.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.210
- I feel so old, and a rotary phone.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:43.750
They're like, what is a phone at home?

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:44.720
I've only had cell phones.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:45.680
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh, right?

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.270
- But they're, it's amazing
seeing them come out,

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.440
handle the pressure of
being in front of millions

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.520
of people watching at home.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.480
But, even the stories we
hear, there was a kid,

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.600
Christopher Harding Jones,
this unbelievable story.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.810
He has a sensory processing disorder,

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:04.840
but his dad was diagnosed with
lung cancer six years ago,

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:06.830
given six months to live.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:10.210
And the dad said, "I can't
control how long I live

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:11.830
but I can control how wide I live.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.550
I wanna live wide and do everything."

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:16.180
And the dad ended up being
around for three years,

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:20.302
but passed away, and the kid just said,

00:03:20.302 --> 00:03:21.910
"Growing up I always
watched "Ninja Warrior",

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.310
and I thought, I wanna live
wide, I want to go try this."

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:25.480
So he's out there-

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.410
- What a legacy-
- Running on the show-

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:27.400
- To leave behind.
- But keeping his

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.450
dad's memory alive.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:29.910
- Yeah.
- And for so many people,

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:32.090
I think, who are
confronted with, you know,

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:34.710
our own mortality, that idea of, you know,

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:37.250
there are ways you live
on past your time here

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.617
by by how you influence people.

00:03:38.617 --> 00:03:40.570
And I thought it was
just a beautiful message.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:41.403
- Yeah.
- I get to,

00:03:41.403 --> 00:03:44.510
I must have cried 23 times this season.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:47.260
We had two proposals, both yeses.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.010
It's really cool being a part of a show

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:50.810
where the performances on the course

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:52.160
are just the beginning and-

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:52.993
- Yeah.
- The obstacles

00:03:52.993 --> 00:03:55.440
people overcome in life, we, you know,

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:56.630
particularly during this pandemic,

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.050
I think we've all been
confronted with the challenges,

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:00.570
but seeing how some people

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:01.780
just choose to fight-
- Overcome.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:02.737
- And overcome it.
- Yeah.

00:04:02.737 --> 00:04:04.080
- And I think it's so inspiring,

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.297
now I'm not working out,
but it does inspire you.

00:04:06.297 --> 00:04:07.280
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.480
It does inspire you, I'm not gonna,

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:09.526
I'm not getting carried away.

00:04:09.526 --> 00:04:10.820
- (laughing) I love that though,

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:12.760
that they, you can see
people, like how we,

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.590
you see humanity like
really push themselves

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:15.465
and see what we're capable of.

00:04:15.465 --> 00:04:16.420
It's really cool.
- It is, and I think

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.476
that's what we've needed,

00:04:17.476 --> 00:04:20.470
is this idea of you see
someone do something and,

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.820
what's cool is when they
surprise themselves,

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.900
and do something that
maybe they didn't even know

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.050
what they're capable of.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:26.883
And I think especially

00:04:26.883 --> 00:04:28.140
for the young kids-
- Sense of accomplishment.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:29.490
- You see them have a moment

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.773
that could shape the rest of their lives.

